{
  "title": "MapLevelProvider",
  "description": "Produces the runtime TileMap for one level - the single seam where a source format meets the format-neutral world runtime. Anything awaitable is accepted, so a provider can hand back a LoaderScope.load queue directly. The returned map becomes **owned by that level runtime**, which destroys it on unload. Return a map built for this load; handing back a shared map (an entry of an eagerly converted document, say) makes the runtime destroy an object other code still holds.",
